  "headline": "Bailey blasts to 79 as Grim clings on to a 16-point lead",
  "summary": "David Bailey was Gameweek 9’s clear star with 79 points, surging three places into fourth, while Mark Horton’s 70 kept the pressure firmly on Louis Grimoldby. Grim FC remains top on 629, but Vespa Mo Pedro is only 16 points back and the chasing pack is closing fast.",
  "report": "David Bailey owned Gameweek 9. Dave’s Dream Team posted a league-best 79 points with no hits, beating Mark Horton’s 70 and olly barnes’ 68 to manager of the week honours. That haul launched Bailey three places up to fourth on 597, just four points behind Grasshoppers and six ahead of Will Finney’s 0v3rf1tt3d.h5.\n\nAt the top, Louis Grimoldby stays put in first with Grim FC on 629, but it was not a serene week. A 55-point wildcard was enough to retain the lead, yet Mark Horton sliced into the gap with 70 and now sits on 613, 16 points off first. olly barnes also climbed two places to third on 601, while Bailey’s charge means the top five is beginning to look properly congested: only four points separate third and fourth, six separate fourth and fifth, and George Foy is just five behind Will Finney in sixth.\n\nHorton’s captaincy call was the one to admire. N.Jackson delivered 9 points with the armband, while 17 managers put their faith in Haaland and received just 2 points. Jamie Mitchell had the roughest captain moment of all as João Pedro returned 0. Elsewhere, Rogers also scored 9, Palmer delivered 8, and the increasingly familiar Kinsky, Raya and Calafiori returns offered useful points across the league.\n\nBailey’s 79 included a tidy 8-point differential from Ajer, owned by him alone. Abi Speight, up three places after 53 points, had Rice’s 8 and Kelleher’s 7, while Hayley Phelan shared Rice and also had Havertz’s 9. George Foy was the other Havertz owner, amy warden had Robertson’s 8 to herself, and Hill’s 6 was shared by Abi Speight and Will Finney.\n\nFor Grimoldby, the 29 points left on the bench will sting rather more than the 55 from the wildcard will soothe. Finney’s free hit produced 51, exactly around the league average of 51.2, while nobody took a points hit. At the other end, Ali Smith’s Bamba No. 8 managed 27, collected the wooden spoon and fell five places; Tim Chodha dropped three after 48, and Finney slipped two despite his 51.\n\nThe league average of 51.2 comfortably beat the global average of 44, but Bailey’s 79 was the BFL benchmark rather than an assault on the global high of 122. Paul Alexis remains the league’s hottest recent manager with 209 points across the last three gameweeks, while Georg Coakley has 135 over the same stretch. With 29 gameweeks remaining, Horton’s season-best 116 from Gameweek 2 is still the score to beat—but the race for the summit is now very much alive.",
